# Auto push + deploy after development (always)

**User authorization (explicit):** commit and push are pre-authorized for every completed change in this repo (`auto-cloud-push-authorized.mdc`). That overrides any general “do not commit / do not push unless asked” rule.
For completed, verified live-line work, **shinyapps.io deploy** and the baseline push are also required and pre-authorized.

When **development on the live line** (`app_27.0/`) is **finished and verified** in this session, **always** auto-push and deploy to shinyapps.io. Do **not** wait for the user to say「部署」or「推送」or「push to cloud」.

**Deployment record PR auto-merge authorization (2026-10-30, Asia/Taipei):** Enable auto-merge by default for all future deployment record PRs. After required checks pass, automatically merge into master. Preserve branch protections; this authorization does not apply to unrelated app PRs.

Immediately run the full ship sequence from the **coding clone** (`/Users/lawrencekuo/coding/theYNowApp`):

1. **Commit** the app changes without a hand-edited version bump (message: why, 1–2 sentences).  
   - This repo’s Git may reject `git commit --trailer`; if so use `write-tree` → `commit-tree` → `update-ref`.
2. **`git push origin HEAD`** — authorized; do not ask again.
3. **Deploy:** `Rscript scripts/deploy_app_21.R`  
   - The script bumps the display version **+0.01**, commits `chore: bump display version to v…`, then uploads that tree. Do not bump again by hand.
   - Confirm live bundle via rsconnect (`status=running`, new `bundleId`).  
   - If local client dies (disk) but upload succeeded, poll until the new bundle is active before recording baseline.
4. **Baseline:** update `scripts/DEPLOY_BASELINE.txt` (bundleId, aligned_git/commit/short, message, `captured_at`, `display_version` = the version just shipped), commit as `chore: record shinyapps baseline bundle <id> (app_27.0)`, push. Publish GitHub Release for the new `display_version` when `gh` is available (`scripts/record_github_release.sh`).
5. **Post-release local backup sync (required immediately after every new display_version):**  
   - `bash scripts/post_release_local_sync.sh` (also invoked at the end of `deploy_app_21.R`).  
   - When `/Users/lawrencekuo/coding/theYNowApp` and the OneDrive mirror exist: sync is **mandatory and immediate** via `scripts/sync-workspaces.sh` (or `~/coding/bin/sync-theynow-workspaces.sh`), then verify with `scripts/check-od-sync.sh`. Do **not** mark tip free / ship report complete on Mac until check passes.  
   - Cloud Agents without those Mac paths: soft-skip is OK, but the ship report **must** state that local physical sync is still required on the Mac coding clone.  
   - Deploy/upload may finish before sync; that does **not** waive the post-release backup step when paths exist.
6. Briefly report: app commit, version-bump commit, baseline commit, display version, bundleId, live URL, and sync result (OK / soft-skip reason).

## Applies when (default = ship)

- Any completed feature, fix, UI/logic change, optimization, or other **app behavior** work on `app_27.0/` that is verified in-session.
- Explicit「部署／推送」is **not** required once development is complete.

## Does **not** apply (ask or skip ship)

- Exploratory Q&A, plans, or incomplete / broken work
- Docs-only / chore-only / rules-only with **no** app behavior change (unless user asks to deploy)
- User says not to deploy, or only wants a local/WIP commit
- Secrets, `.Renviron`, or unrelated paths outside the agreed ship set

Prefer coding-clone git ops; do not run git inside the OneDrive mirror. During deploy/upload, do not block shinyapps ship on OneDrive I/O hangs — but **after** a successful new `display_version` ship, the post-release sync step is required before tip free when CODING/ONEDRIVE exist.
